  "goodToKnow": "Die Baracke is a simple, temporary building, usually of wood: Holzbaracken for workers, refugees or soldiers, and colloquially a shack. Many post-war schools and offices began in Baracken. Military barracks in the proper sense are die Kaserne. In Nazi camps, prisoners were held in Baracken, so the word can carry heavy associations. Plural: die Baracken."
